# These are the default settings for the practical benchmark

# A directory is perfectly fine with the default settings
# For real measures using a real TLD zone, a persistent storage with hundred of gigabytes or terabytes of space must be considered
# Depending on the parameters, the run can takes hours to days.
PREFIX="/tmp/registry"

# The TLD that will be used. The default is "eu" and the sources will generate a small stub if needed.
ORIGIN="eu"
# The zone file name for the TLD, to be found in the zonesign directory
# You can provide your own zone file provided it's an unsigned NSEC3 zone without any DNSKEY present
# The scripts will sign it NSEC3-OPTOUT for each selected algorithm
ZONEFILENAME="$ORIGIN.zone"

# The algorithms that'll be used by the benchmark
#
# Possible groups are:
#
# ALGORITHMS_2O26 ALGORITHMS_TRAD ALGORITHMS_DILITHIUM ALGORITHMS_FALCON ALGORITHMS_SPHINCS ALGORITHMS_MAYO ALGORITHMS_CROSS
#
# ALGORITHMS_2O26 This is the recommended list.  Look inside the 'run' script to know more.
#
ALGORITHMS="$ALGORITHMS_2O26"

# Signatures iterations
#
# During the benchmark, signatures are executed N times.
# For the example setup, this value is set to 2.
# Bigger values may takes days or weeks to execute.
#
# For reference, on a i7-12850HX, a DNSSEC_BENCHMARK_SIGNATURES_COUNT=10 will take about 40 minutes.
#
DNSSEC_BENCHMARK_SIGNATURES_COUNT=2

# The settings below this line are probably best left untouched.

# YADIFA 3.0.9 will be cloned and used locally
YADIFA_GIT="https://github.com/yadifa/yadifa.git"
YADIFA_GIT_TAG="v3.0.9"
YADIFA_SRC="$SCRIPT_DIR/yadifa"
YADIFA_BUILDDIR="$SCRIPT_DIR/yadifa-build"

YADIFA="$YADIFA_BUILDDIR/bin/yadifa/yadifa"
YADIFAD="$YADIFA_BUILDDIR/sbin/yadifad/yadifad"

GLIBCHOOKS_SRC="$SCRIPT_DIR/glibchooks"
GLIBCHOOKS_BUILDDIR="$SCRIPT_DIR/glibchooks-build"
PRELOAD="$PREFIX/lib/libglibchooks.so"

ZONEDIR="$PREFIX/zonesign"
DESTDIR="$PREFIX/quantum"
